(*"person_organization_schema.person_organization_select"
The **person_organization_select** type allows for the designation of an <<express:person_organization_schema.organization,organization>>, a <<express:person_organization_schema.person,person>> or a <<express:person_organization_schema.person_and_organization,person_and_organization>>.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address"
An **address** is the information necessary for communicating, using one or more communication methods.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.address.__example"
A generic attribute named "LinkedIn" with a value of "Fred.Bloggs" could be used to add a LinkedIn account to address information.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.address.__note"
In addition to the attributes defined in *address* additional generic attributes may be assigned using <<express:basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_assignment,generic_attribute_assignment>>.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.address.internal_location"
an organization-defined address for internal mail delivery. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address.street_number"
the number of a location on a street. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address.street"
the name of a street. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address.postal_box"
the number of a postal box. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address.town"
the name of a town. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address.region"
the name of a region. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.address.region.__example"
The counties of Great Britain and the states of the United States of America are examples of regions.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.address.postal_code"
the code that is used by the **country**'s postal service. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address.country"
the name of a country. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address.facsimile_number"
the number at which facsimiles may be received. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address.telephone_number"
the number at which telephone calls may be received. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address.electronic_mail_address"
the electronic address at which electronic mail may be received. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address.telex_number"
the number at which telex messages may be received. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> that specifies the name of the location identified by the **address**.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.address.name.__example"
"White House", "Buckingham Palace", "Kremlin".
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.address.url"
the text that specifies the uniform resource locator associated with the **address**.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.address.url.__example"
URLs are used to identify items such as world wide web sites and file transfer protocol (FTP) servers.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.address.url.__note"
The format of uniform resource locators is defined in IETF RFC 1738 [4].
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.address.wr:WR1"
At least one of the attributes shall have a value.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.address.wr:WR1.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in annex E.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.organization"
An **organization** is an administrative structure.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.organization.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **organization**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.organization.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.organization.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **organization** is known.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.organization.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **organization**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.organization_relationship"
An **organization_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the entity data type <<express:person_organization_schema.organization,organization>> with a description of their relationship.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.organization_relationship.__example"
Each department of an enterprise, and the enterprise itself, may be regarded as individual organizations. The fact that the departments are a part of the whole enterprise may be represented using this entity.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.organization_relationship.__note"
The role of *organization_relationship* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.organization_relationship.__note"
Relationships represented using this entity may be parent child relationship. Annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity specify whether or not the relationship is directed.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.organization_relationship.__note"
This entity, together with the <<express:person_organization_schema.organization,organization>> entity, is based on the relationship template that is described in annex E.3.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.organization_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **organization_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.organization_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **organization_relationship**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.organization_relationship.relating_organization"
one of the instances of <<express:person_organization_schema.organization,organization>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


