(*"person_organization_schema.person"
A **person** is an individual human being.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.person.__example"
For example a generic attribute list named "Previous name" with a value of ["Honourific":"Mr", "Given name":"Fred", "Family Name":"Blogs"] may be assigned.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.person.__note"
In addition to the attributes defined in *person* additional lists of attributes may be assigned using <<express:basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_list_assignment,generic_attribute_list_assignment>>.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.person.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **person**.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.person.id.__example"
In the USA a person's *id* would be his or her social security number whereas in the United Kingdom it would be his or her national insurance number.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.person.id.__note"
The identification of a person is usually context dependent.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.person.id.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.person.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"person_organization_schema.person.last_name"
the **person**'s surname. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.person.first_name"
the first element of the **person**'s list of forenames. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.person.middle_names"
the **person**'s other forenames, if there are any. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.person.prefix_titles"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that specifies the **person**'s social or professional standing and appear before his or her names. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.person.suffix_titles"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that specifies the **person**'s social or professional standing and appear after his or her names. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"person_organization_schema.person.wr:WR1"
Either the last name, first name or the last and first name shall be defined.
*)


